If you look closely at history, something striking appears: generations don’t just pass through time — they move in rhythm. One rises, leaves its mark, and the next ____(71)____ builds on it or pushes back. Time may seem like a straight line, but if you slow down, you’ll see it’s more of a cycle. Each generation inherits a world shaped by those before it — absorbing values, lessons, and expectations — and is molded by defining events ____(72)____ wars, crises, and cultural shifts. These experiences shape how we think, what we believe, and who we become. As we grow older, we start to question what we were taught and look for better ways forward. That’s when the cycle turns again: ____(73)____ generation challenges the old and creates the new. Eventually, their ideas become ____(74)____ . It’s a dance of influence and rebellion, inheritance and reinvention. Once you notice the rhythm, you can’t unsee it — it explains not just the past but the present and what’s yet to come. This generational rhythm moves ____(75)____ four recurring stages: revolution, stability, pragmatism, and crisis — before beginning again.','["as", "to", "like", "through"]'::jsonb,2,array[2]::smallint[],'["ยกตัวอย่าง defining events like wars, crises, and cultural shifts (like = เช่น)"]'::jsonb,'["ไม่ถูก as ไม่ใช้นำตัวอย่างแบบนี้ (ต้องเป็น such as)", "ไม่ถูก to ไม่สื่อการยกตัวอย่าง", "ถูก like = เช่น", "ไม่ถูก through = ผ่าน ความหมายไม่เข้า"]'::jsonb,'{"after": "72. เลือกคำตอบที่เหมาะสมที่สุดสำหรับช่องว่าง ____(72)____", "topic": "3.1", "n": 72}'::jsonb,'imported_m6','imported',false,null,'Exam Gym ม.6 · 5620e4c',2569,'eng:69-72');
