Conversation 4
Situation: A student talks to a career counselor
Counselor: Hi, Ploy. Come in and have a seat. ____(21)____
Ploy: I can’t decide what to study at university. My parents want me to study medicine, but I’m more interested in design.
Counselor: I see. ____(22)____
Ploy: I love drawing, and I’ve won two poster competitions. But I’m worried design jobs don’t pay well.
Counselor: That’s a common concern. Actually, UX designers in tech companies earn quite well. ____(23)____
Ploy: That’s a good idea. But how do I talk to my parents about it?
